157-
158:- **Page object methods** are named for what is on the page (`enterBoat`, `clickBook`, `notification`) and return what the user sees — strings, numbers, lists of row texts — never components. Then the story can't reach past them into the UI.
159-- **Actor methods** are the verbs and questions of the use case (`books`, `cancels`, `approves`; `wasToldThat`, `isOffered`). An actor whose story crosses views holds a page object per view, all over the same window.
160-- **When a story needs a step that doesn't exist yet**, add the verb to the actor first and the page object method under it. Don't add a locator to the test method "just this once".
161-- **A composite used on several views**, such as an address form, gets its own page object that the views' page objects reuse, or a custom locator; see [beyond-the-browser.md](beyond-the-browser.md).
162-- **A page reload or a second tab** is a new window of the same user: keep the actor's `BrowserlessUserContext` and call `newWindow()` again. Session state carries over; the UI state starts fresh.
